This extension adds Red Faction Guerrilla Re-Mars-tered modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Automatically installs Mod Manager.[/summary]

[b][size=2]The classic version of RFG can also be used with this extension. Another version of Mod Manager tool will download from [url=https://www.factionfiles.com/ff.php?action=file&amp;id=3863]HERE[/url] if you are not on Re-Mars-tered version.[/size][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a "mod manager re-mars-tered.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a "modmanager.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Mods with a "modinfo.xml" file install to the "mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatically downloads and installs [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/redfactionguerrillaremarstered/mods/10]Mod Manager[/url]﻿﻿﻿﻿, which is required by most mods. This tool must be run from the Dashboard after installing mods with Vortex.[/*]
[*]Includes mod type to install mods to the game's root folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Red Faction Guerrilla Re-Mars-tered mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Mod Manager:

Recognised when the archive contains a "mod manager re-mars-tered.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Manager Legacy:

Recognised when the archive contains a "modmanager.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "modinfo.xml" file.

  Installs to: "mods"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
